      "text": "### Four Defining Structures"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-MOLLUSCA.md#007",
      "path": [
        "05-MOLLUSCA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:animal-phylogeny:05-mollusca, git-history:animal-phylogeny:05-mollusca]",
        "canonical_path": "animal-phylogeny/05-MOLLUSCA.md",
        "concepts": "[mollusca]",
        "current_path": "animal-phylogeny/05-MOLLUSCA.md",
        "id": "maxim:animal-phylogeny:mollusca",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "animal-phylogeny",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[mollusca]",
        "section": "animal-phylogeny",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Mollusca - The Second Most Species-Rich Animal Phylum",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n1. MANTLE\n   ┌────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n   │ Dorsal fold of body wall                   │\n   │ Secretes shell (periostracum + calcite     │\n   │   layers: prismatic + nacreous)            │\n   │ Encloses mantle cavity                     │\n   │ Gas exchange, waste removal, gametes       │\n   └────────────────────────────────────────────┘"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-MOLLUSCA.md#008",
      "path": [
        "05-MOLLUSCA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:animal-phylogeny:05-mollusca, git-history:animal-phylogeny:05-mollusca]",
        "canonical_path": "animal-phylogeny/05-MOLLUSCA.md",
        "concepts": "[mollusca]",
        "current_path": "animal-phylogeny/05-MOLLUSCA.md",
        "id": "maxim:animal-phylogeny:mollusca",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "animal-phylogeny",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[mollusca]",
        "section": "animal-phylogeny",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Mollusca - The Second Most Species-Rich Animal Phylum",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "2. FOOT\n   ┌────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n   │ Muscular, ventral, highly modified         │\n   │ Gastropod: flat creeping sole              │\n   │ Bivalve: wedge for burrowing               │\n   │ Cephalopod: highly modified → funnel + arms│\n   └────────────────────────────────────────────┘"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-MOLLUSCA.md#009",
      "path": [
        "05-MOLLUSCA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:animal-phylogeny:05-mollusca, git-history:animal-phylogeny:05-mollusca]",
        "canonical_path": "animal-phylogeny/05-MOLLUSCA.md",
        "concepts": "[mollusca]",
        "current_path": "animal-phylogeny/05-MOLLUSCA.md",
        "id": "maxim:animal-phylogeny:mollusca",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "animal-phylogeny",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[mollusca]",
        "section": "animal-phylogeny",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Mollusca - The Second Most Species-Rich Animal Phylum",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "3. RADULA (absent in Bivalvia)\n   ┌────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n   │ Ribbon of chitin teeth on muscular base    │\n   │ Moves back and forth like rasp/file        │\n   │ Tooth row patterns vary by feeding mode:   │\n   │   Herbivore: many small teeth (docoglossat)│\n   │   Carnivore: fewer, larger teeth           │\n   │   Boring (whelks): drill through shell     │\n   │   Cone snail: harpoon-like (venomous)      │\n   └────────────────────────────────────────────┘"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-MOLLUSCA.md#010",
      "path": [
        "05-MOLLUSCA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:animal-phylogeny:05-mollusca, git-history:animal-phylogeny:05-mollusca]",
        "canonical_path": "animal-phylogeny/05-MOLLUSCA.md",
        "concepts": "[mollusca]",
        "current_path": "animal-phylogeny/05-MOLLUSCA.md",
        "id": "maxim:animal-phylogeny:mollusca",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "animal-phylogeny",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[mollusca]",
        "section": "animal-phylogeny",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Mollusca - The Second Most Species-Rich Animal Phylum",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "4. CTENIDIA (gills in mantle cavity)\n   ┌────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n   │ Ancestral gill form: bipectinate (feather) │\n   │ Highly modified in bivalves → filter plate │\n   │ Lost in land snails (replaced by lung)     │\n   └────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```"
    },
