        "root_concepts": "[mollusca]",
        "section": "animal-phylogeny",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Mollusca - The Second Most Species-Rich Animal Phylum",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nMOLLUSCAN SHELL CROSS-SECTION\n+------------------------------------------+\n|  Periostracum   Organic protein (quinone)|\n|                 Outermost, protective    |\n+------------------------------------------+\n|  Prismatic     Calcite or aragonite       |\n|  layer         Columnar crystals          |\n+------------------------------------------+\n|  Nacreous      Aragonite platelets +     |\n|  layer         protein (conchiolin)      |\n|  (mother of    Iridescent interference   |\n|   pearl)       NACRE                     |\n+------------------------------------------+\n|  Interior      Contact with mantle tissue |\n+------------------------------------------+"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-MOLLUSCA.md#013",
      "path": [
        "05-MOLLUSCA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:animal-phylogeny:05-mollusca, git-history:animal-phylogeny:05-mollusca]",
        "canonical_path": "animal-phylogeny/05-MOLLUSCA.md",
        "concepts": "[mollusca]",
