        "section": "animal-phylogeny",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Mollusca - The Second Most Species-Rich Animal Phylum",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "NACRE FORMATION:\n  Mantle epithelium secretes calcium carbonate platelets\n  Each platelet: ~0.5 μm thick, 5–20 μm wide\n  Stacked in offset columns → brick-wall structure\n  Light interferes between platelets → iridescence\n  Pearl: nacre deposited around irritant (parasite or bead)\n  Cultured pearl: bead inserted → mantle wrap → nacre layers\n```"
    },
