        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Mollusca - The Second Most Species-Rich Animal Phylum",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "BEFORE TORSION:        AFTER TORSION:\nHead   ──► Anus        Head   ──► Anus (above head!)\n                       Gills (now above head, facing forward)\n                       Mantle cavity (now anterior)"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-MOLLUSCA.md#020",
      "path": [
        "05-MOLLUSCA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:animal-phylogeny:05-mollusca, git-history:animal-phylogeny:05-mollusca]",
        "canonical_path": "animal-phylogeny/05-MOLLUSCA.md",
        "concepts": "[mollusca]",
        "current_path": "animal-phylogeny/05-MOLLUSCA.md",
        "id": "maxim:animal-phylogeny:mollusca",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "animal-phylogeny",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[mollusca]",
        "section": "animal-phylogeny",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Mollusca - The Second Most Species-Rich Animal Phylum",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "CONSEQUENCE:\n  The mouth and anus end up near each other (above head)\n  Gills face forward → better water flow\n  Mantle cavity (with gills + osphradia) → over head\n  Problem: fouling of gills by own waste → \"sanitation problem\"\n  Solutions evolved: slit shells, holes (limpets), operculum"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-MOLLUSCA.md#021",
      "path": [
        "05-MOLLUSCA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
